                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "please elaborate more on this, people outside in community might not know what this really means."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 349,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thu Nguyen",
                        "email": "thu@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "ThuBaNguyen"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we use new instead of `reinterpret_cast`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 349,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "no @thu@os.amperecomputing.com, Using placement new with a const type (i.e., trying to construct an object into a const memory location) is usually problematic and generally not allowed, because placement new implies that you're about to write to the specified memory address, which contradicts the idea of const."
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 369,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "shouldn't we ensure that we have space in table for getting another tlv ? \n\n`if (table.size() - pos < recordLen + tlvLen)` and bail out as error ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 369,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 371,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "shouldn't this be other way round ?\n\n`if ((le16toh(recordSetSrc->record_set_id) != rsi && rsi != 0))`\n\ncomparing `record_set_id` in little-endian format with `rsi`, which is likely in host format. Using htole16() here flips rsi to little-endian before comparing it to a value that's already in LE \u2014 that doesn't make sense. You should convert the LE field to host format before comparing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 371,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 383,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "shouldn't we ensure that we have another record before we do this ? \n\n`if (table.size() - pos < sizeof(struct pldm_fru_record_data_format))` ? then bail out ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "libpldmresponder/fru.cpp",
                    "line": 383,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
